Triaged. No files modified.

1. `test_cancel_keeps_alive_then_aclose_reaps_tree`

Root cause: environment. The test starts the real pi-kernel sidecar. On this checkout, `default_pi_kernel_entry()` falls back to `packages/pi-kernel/src/index.ts` because `dist/index.js` is absent, and `packages/pi-kernel/node_modules` is also absent. Node exits before `ready` with `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND` for `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent`, imported by [runner.ts](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/pi-kernel/src/runner.ts:30).

Verdict: ENVIRONMENT.

Minimal fix: run `npm run setup && npm run build` in `packages/pi-kernel`, or make this test skip when the built sidecar/dependency install is missing.

2. `test_no_contamination_non_anchored_standard_withholds_str_replace_and_plan_step`

Root cause: stale expectation. The test expects only `{"plan_step", "file_str_replace"}`, but [ModelExecutionPolicy.withheld_tools](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/core/src/disco/core/llm/exec_policy.py:66) also withholds `exact_replace` when `anchored_edit=False`. That matches the newer CD-TOOLS-2 behavior; tools tests already assert `exact_replace` is an anchored-edit tool.

Verdict: STALE TEST.

Minimal fix: update [test_policy_consistency.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/agent-server/tests/test_policy_consistency.py:326) to expect `{"plan_step", "file_str_replace", "exact_replace"}` and update the assertion text/docstring.

3. `test_run_checks_cascades_skip_when_config_fails`

Root cause: stale monkeypatch target. The test patches `verify._build_runtime`, but `verify.run_checks` is re-exported from `_setup_checks`, so its global `_build_runtime` is still `disco.agent_server.verify._setup_checks._build_runtime`. The fake no-driver runtime is never used. On this box, real config passes with `driver-minimax -> http://localhost:8080/v1`, so the test hits live checks instead of the cascade path.

Verdict: STALE TEST.

Minimal fix: patch `disco.agent_server.verify._setup_checks._build_runtime` instead, or import `_setup_checks` in the test and run/patch that module directly. The cascade logic itself works when `_setup_checks._build_runtime` is patched.
